    "description": "Dave Lombardo's cymbal choice for \"The Gathering\" sessions reflected a shift from the Paiste RUDE/2002 series that had defined his early Slayer recordings toward Zildjian's A series — hand-hammered, warm, complex cymbals with more overtone complexity and musical character than Paiste's deliberately aggressive RUDE series.\n\nThe Zildjian A series suited Morrisound Recording's sonic environment. Where Paiste RUDE cymbals cut with raw, almost harsh aggression — perfect for Reign in Blood's monolithic sonic assault — the A series delivered a more nuanced attack with complex decay. In the context of \"The Gathering's\" death-influenced arrangements, that complexity worked with the music rather than against it.\n\nThe A 14\" hi-hats provided warm, articulate patterns across tempos that ranged from mid-paced thrash to near-blast territory. Testament's guitarists were executing technically demanding riff patterns, and Lombardo's hi-hat work needed to complement rather than compete with that texture. The A series' hand-hammered variation produced a more human, responsive sound than computer-assisted designs — each stroke slightly different from the last, maintaining musical interest across extended passages.\n\nThe three-crash configuration — 16\", 18\", 19\" — offered Lombardo graduated options for the album's dynamic range. The 18\" China added the cutting, aggressive accent that the album's most aggressive passages demanded: \"3 Days in Darkness\" in particular features China usage that mirrors the guitar's percussive, low-register attack patterns.",
